;; Reviewed 2026-10-11 by the user (written by Claude, from the design,
;; the MACRO manual, LLVM's code generator and the guest runs). Why this
;; is right:
;; - Phase 16 step 5 (section 16, proposal 7): a structured constant
;;   (Phase 14) is data in POC_CONST, L_CONST_<n>, one for each value
;;   the module uses, as LLVM makes a private constant global of each
;;   module that uses one (an imported one too, from its .sym). Each is
;;   .ALIGN QUAD, the most a variable needs, and is used as a variable of
;;   its type would be: MOVC3 from it to assign (CopyAll, GridCorners),
;;   its address in the argument list for a value parameter, which the
;;   callee copies, an open array or a read-only one (SumVector,
;;   GridCorners).
;; - Its bytes are a variable's, at MemoryLayout's offsets (section 4):
;;   all's base field tag first (84, "T"), then s at 1, i at 2, l at 4,
;;   h at 8 (a quadword, low longword first, as HalfText writes an
;;   immediate: -5000000000 is ^XFFFFFFFE_D5FA0E00), b at 16 and three
;;   bytes of padding, set at 20 ({0, 31}), set64 at 24 ({1, 63}: the
;;   low and high longwords), r at 32 and lr at 36 as .F_FLOATING and
;;   .G_FLOATING of RealConstant's text, which MACRO rounds as it does an
;;   immediate, p at 44 (NIL, 0), name at 48 ("abc", then zeros), and
;;   zeros to the record's size, 56.
;; - An array's elements one after another, those not given zero:
;;   vector's [0..1] and [4]; grid's records, the second all zero.
;; - ConstOut, run on the guest under -O2 and -OC, prints what the LLVM
;;   build prints (output.expected), these constants used from another
;;   module and literals of its own included.
